WEBVTT

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.720
Seven percent increase in density.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.320
Heart rate confirmed.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.760
Engaging the separation process.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.110
The Persona is part of one's spirit.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:33.730
It's essentially impossible to
separate from the physical body.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.750
Some sacrifices are inevitable...
but I've finally found a way.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:45.120
Collecting A Latents... This has now
become something far more significant.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.370
kanjouni aragau nayo
Don't fight back your emotions

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:05.740
sono ashiwo tomenna
Don't ever stop

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:09.800
taoreru nowa mada hayaize
It's too soon to fall down

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:11.850
Breakin' through
Breakin' through

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.620
uchinukeyo
Pierce through

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.920
yamiwo hurihodoki
Free yourself from darkness

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.010
tadoritsuku bashowa hitotsusa
There is only one destination

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.220
hurueru sora
Quaking sky

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:29.590
kazewa naniwo tsugeru
What is the wind telling me?

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:35.700
tadashii datoka soujanai toka
Right or wrong

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.740
kudaranai ronsouwa
Nonsensical arguments

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.310
kieya shinai kedo
Never go away

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:45.950
shinjita kotowo shinjinuku koto
Believe what you believe in

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:49.080
sono sakini bokurawa
At the end of it all

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.590
hikari mitsukeru darou
We will find the light

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:56.690
saa tokihanate ima
Now is the time to release it

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:59.690
kanjouni aragau nayo
Don't fight back your emotions

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:01.900
sono ashiwo tomenna
Don't ever stop

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:05.920
taoreru nowa mada hayaize
It's too soon to fall down

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.000
Breakin' through
Breakin' through

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.740
uchinukeyo
Pierce through

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:12.110
yamiwo hurihodoki
Free yourself from darkness

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:16.130
tadoritsuku bashowa hitotsusa
There is only one destination

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:32.560
All right. The next test will include
everything up to page 103.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:33.830
What?

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.660
What?
Seriously?

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.890
There, there. That's it for today.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.580
Ooh, what is it? A date?

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:49.640
With who?

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.580
Huh? It's not like that...

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:57.210
Oh, isn't this for the place
that closed down recently?

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.950
You didn't go to it?

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:04.080
Well... the kid who sold this
ticket to me disappeared...

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:09.420
He was happy to be able to play at their last event.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.760
He was supposed to be the opening performance.

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.000
What do you mean "disappeared?"

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:20.010
You've heard of the missing kids that were
involved in Shadow Extraction, right?

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.910
I hope Takashi isn't involved in that, too...

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:27.080
I'm starting to worry about this whole thing.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:32.120
Takashi? Isn't that who you got into a fight
with at the beginning of the school year?

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:34.780
Yeah, Okazaki Takashi.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:36.490
Okazaki?

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:39.660
He was in my class last year.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.460
He was really good at singing and playing guitar.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:42.760
Is Okazaki?

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.470
Kanzato-kun?

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.870
Do you know him, too?

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:48.770
Okazaki Takashi
Tasaka Yumi

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:54.380
No... um, I knew a kid with the
same name at my old school.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.850
They're probably not the same guy, though...

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.810
Hah, it's unlikely.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:04.210
And I was gonna go listen to his
bad singing to show my support...

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:06.650
I'm sure he'll come back soon...

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.080
Sure.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.740
What do you think?

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.980
I can't really see clearly.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:32.540
May I?

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:33.810
Right here.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.050
See? Here... Right here. Look.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:39.450
That's not it.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:43.190
We already looked there. At the actual scene.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:47.520
There.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.220
That's...

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.800
Make a copy of it.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.170
What? But the Chief said...

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:54.240
Doesn't matter.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.100
Yes, it does.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:00.510
Just do it. Plus, those two girls in there...

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:04.280
Doesn't matter if they're "frail little
girls." Make sure you watch them closely.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.250
I've been on it...

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:11.250
That afro kid and the Chief's brother, too.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:14.850
What about that... list?

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:18.630
He said he didn't find it.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.820
Of course...

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.860
He sure is bad at lying.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.200
Unlike his older brother...

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:41.880
Even though he was bad, he kept singing...

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:47.220
So he got that stuff... You know? Mikorin got it, too.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:48.320
A polyp?

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.520
Yeah, that.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:52.050
That's as close as he got to
being a professional singer.

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:56.330
Are you serious?

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.860
Sweet! You owe me a drink.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.270
Man, today isn't my day.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.910
No way. It's all skill.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:05.300
Yeah, right.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:14.620
Anyway, an audition was held
right after his throat surgery.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.720
It was at this place that's been
popular among locals for a long time.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.790
Some pros got their start there, too.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:22.420
People called that place the Rocker Mecca.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:30.320
Takashi and his band members dreamed
of playing on the stage there, too.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:35.870
But he was told to refrain from singing
for at least a month by the doctor.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:40.700
I told his band members not to
tell Takashi about the audition.

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:43.110
Of course, he found out right away.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:48.020
"Stop being a fool!"

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.880
That's his favorite phrase.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.050
"I was about to make the
biggest mistake of my life."

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.210
He was furious.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:01.200
He was right, though.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:06.330
I thought I was doing good for him,
but nobody wants to be lied to.

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:10.360
Only he could decide whether or
not he was gonna do it for himself.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:16.140
I wish he had gotten the chance to sing.

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:19.310
Not that anyone would enjoy listening to him, but...

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.390
Okazaki Takashi
Tasaka Yumi

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:40.000
Jun...

00:07:42.770 --> 00:08:05.990
Jun!

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.290
Shin-oniichan.

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:13.220
Where do you think you're going now?

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.500
I can feel it.

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:19.300
The sound.

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:24.470
The voice.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:36.350
It's in pain.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:38.260
H-hey.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:00.640
Stop!

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:19.960
Stay here.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:20.970
But...

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:24.910
Just stay here. I'll be back soon.

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:26.900
Niichan!

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.910
What am I doing here?

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:02.170
A theatre?

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:46.410
Well, how did you find this place?

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.990
You're not gonna answer me? ...Sure, I understand.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.390
I was rather rude to you when we first met.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:11:00.560
It's pretty tough. The new Persona
I absorbed just won't calm down.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:05.590
The original owner had built
quite a strong bond here.

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:09.470
I wonder if he wanted to sing a song or something?

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:12.310
Oh, could you have, possibly, known him?

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:14.610
...Are you talking about Okazaki?

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:18.950
Right. That name sounds familiar.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:20.960
Where is he now?

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:24.250
Who knows? Why don't you ask the police?

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:29.900
That's right. Isn't your brother the Chief Officer?

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:31.330
How do you know that?

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:36.000
I didn't wanna make him suffer too much, but...

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.240
Did you kill him... and take it?

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.040
I can't take it unless I kill him.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.040
I'm not like you.

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:44.510
Like me?

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:47.550
So, you really do have no idea.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:50.050
What the hell are you guys!?

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:52.050
Visitors.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:53.350
Do you wanna come with us?

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:55.690
It'll be fun.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:25.450
Looks like he's very interested in you, but...

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.690
that doesn't matter to me.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.650
I'll peel you completely this time.

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:48.870
Niichan!

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:52.110
Jun!? Why did you follow me!?

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:56.080
Jun! Hey!

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.160
Just quiet down.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:38.220
Jun! Let's go!!

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:52.870
I told you not to come...

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:56.000
I have one inside me, too...

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:59.540
You guys didn't say anything
but you both saw it, right?

00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:03.950
My Persona.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.460
About that word you asked about, "Marebito"...

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.490
The one who holds the truths
of mythology and folklore...

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:23.630
It also means Foreign God.

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:30.170
Right... If what you saw is true, that
means research is being carried over...

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:34.680
and is being conducted by some organization
in secret, even after that incident.

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:39.580
It seemed incomplete, but it was
definitely a Complex Persona.

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:44.110
If we trust his words that it's not
something we can investigate officially...

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:47.060
The only place I can think of is
the Department of the Interior...

00:14:47.060 --> 00:14:49.530
Even if we try to take the back
gate, it would be difficult...

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:58.070
I need to talk to you about something.

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:03.070
I found a school in Tokyo where
they allow mid-year transfers.

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:04.050
Just now...

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:07.640
I... was attacked by some
strange people several times.

00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:11.350
Those people, with weird things
that come out from around here...

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.060
It's happened to me, too.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:16.220
Jun, too. You saw it, right?

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:19.180
My friend might have gotten killed.

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:22.920
That's why...

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.060
I told you guys to leave.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:37.080
It's very similar.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:40.040
Yeah... but we're missing something.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:44.680
The Reverse body we always
find at scenes like this.

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:47.560
At least no one died this time...

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:48.540
True...

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:51.790
Just the two of them?

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:55.120
Yes. They went to the back of the campus...

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:56.930
Could it be?

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.830
Are they going to do it?

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:01.100
It?

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:05.670
I need to stop them, once and for all.

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:07.240
Why is Shadow Extraction-?

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:08.140
Why?

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:08.700
Huh?

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:12.300
Why are you so against Shadow Extraction?

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:15.380
I mean... Is it that bad?

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:19.450
Well... it's really dangerous.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:21.790
Have you done it before?

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.380
Well, umm... Let's just go!

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.160
It feels really good...

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:31.020
The hell do you mean, Shin?

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:34.090
I don't just take any jokes, you know?

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:37.040
I'm serious. I saw it.

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:39.170
Saw what?

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.170
Take me there!

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.480
If you keep saying stuff like that, then-

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:45.480
H-hey, hey!

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:48.420
Hey! What do you think you guys are doing!?

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:52.410
He... He says that Takashi is dead!

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:53.180
What?

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:55.850
Is that true, Kanzato-kun?

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:00.120
Yeah, he's probably already...

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:02.050
You!

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:06.260
I saw a Persona.

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:09.560
...I think it belonged to Okazaki.

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:14.470
What? Persona... is that thing that
comes out of your head, right?

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:15.680
Then that means he's still alive...

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:17.640
Not all the time.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:21.850
You're...

00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:25.540
Oh...

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:28.060
Who the hell are you!?

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.460
You know...

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:31.460
He was tough at first.

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:35.230
"Stop being a fool!" Or something...

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:37.600
You bastard!

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:58.610
Kanzato-kun!

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:00.110
Run!

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:03.660
No! Takuro!

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:04.720
Sakakiba-kun!

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:16.400
Geez. He was aggressive, too,
but that changed real quick.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:19.810
He ended up crying and begging...

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:23.070
That was pretty "foolish" of him.

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:27.920
You guys are similar, huh?

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:32.220
Now, stand up. Or are you
gonna keep sleeping there?

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:14.490
Now's my chance!

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:35.980
That was fun. See ya.

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:49.150
I'm sorry.

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:07.000
Shin... Where is?

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:13.710
...I won't forgive him.

00:20:32.670 --> 00:20:33.830
It came out again, huh?

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:36.870
...I forced it out, rather.

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:39.640
I heard the voice...

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:43.210
The painful voice from last night.

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:51.490
It sounded like it was in slightly less agony.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:56.060
...I see.

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:59.860
...Right. I'm sorry, but keep it up. Please.

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:05.430
I'll make it quick. Just listen to me like this.

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:09.870
We're not gonna leave this place.

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:16.320
How could we? There are so many
things we haven't found out...

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:19.780
There are so many that we don't know.

00:21:20.850 --> 00:21:23.320
There are some things that you don't need to know.

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:31.320
It's not...

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:32.860
up to you to decide.

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:38.200
That's it.

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:52.820
omotai kusariwo
The heavy chain

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:58.690
ima hazushite agemashou
I will take it off for you

00:21:58.690 --> 00:22:04.100
jiyuuni naretara
Once you're free

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:10.970
kokowo habataite yukeruwa
You'll be able to fly away

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:17.580
atashiga samatage
I stood in your way

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:25.820
ubatte kita madaminu sekai e
and took that world you haven't seen

00:22:26.390 --> 00:22:30.520
tamerau nonara
If you're going to hesitate

00:22:30.520 --> 00:22:39.370
huriharatte ageru sono udewo
I will free that arm for you

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:43.840
soshite tookue
Then to faraway

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:50.040
dekirudake tookue
As far away as possible

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:53.550
aishiteruno
"I love you"

00:22:53.550 --> 00:22:56.650
ikanaideyo
"Don't leave me"

00:22:56.650 --> 00:23:04.150
koware chaukara
I will break

00:23:13.470 --> 00:23:16.900
Things that wither some day.

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:20.610
Things that break some day.

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:23.940
Things that glow eternally.

00:23:24.910 --> 00:23:26.850
The shielded age.

00:23:27.110 --> 00:23:29.880
A dream reflecting in corrupt eyes.

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:32.220
A familiar smile.

00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:36.250
Even if unseen, even if she is not met.

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:40.760
The warmth remains.
